exit: Some(0)
--- stdout ---
Verify the whole chain from genesis, recomputing every link.

Prints "CHAIN OK: N entries" and exits 0 on success, or "CHAIN BROKEN at seq M" and exits 15 on the first broken link (never the last).

Usage: axon-vm chain verify [OPTIONS] --store <STORE>

Options:
      --store <STORE>
          Path to the chain JSONL file

      --genesis <GENESIS>
          Expected genesis root (`axtcb1-ext:…`). If omitted, the chain's own first entry's `prev_hash` is used (self-consistency check only — pass this explicitly to pin against a known-good R31 boot root)

      --expect-head <EXPECT_HEAD>
          Expected chain tip (`axtcb1-run:…`, as printed by `chain stamp` or `chain show`). AUDIT T31: `--genesis` pins the ROOT, which cannot detect a truncated tail — every prefix of a valid chain is itself a valid chain, so chopping off the last runs still verifies clean. Pin the TIP with this to detect rollback

      --expect-count <EXPECT_COUNT>
          Expected number of entries. Catches a truncation even when the relying party recorded only how many runs it had seen, not the hash

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

